@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### 1. Register a new Project Owner
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Jean Owner",
  "email": "jean.owner@camtrust.test",
  "password": "owner123",
  "confirmPassword": "owner123",
  "role": "property_owner"
}

### 2. Login as Owner (copy the "token" from the response for requests below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jean.owner@camtrust.test",
  "password": "owner123"
}

### 3. Login as Admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@camtrust.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 4. Login as Engineer
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "engineer@camtrust.com",
  "password": "engineer123"
}

### 5. Create a project as Owner (paste Owner token below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/create
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_OWNER_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "Villa Construction - Yaounde",
  "location": "Yaounde, Cameroon",
  "description": "3-bedroom house construction",
  "budget": "15000000",
  "startDate": "2026-09-01"
}

### 6. Reject a project as Admin (paste Admin token + real project id from step 5's response)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/PROJECT_ID/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "status": "Rejected",
  "rejectionReason": "Missing site plan"
}

### 7. Create a second project as Owner (this one we will approve instead)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/create
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_OWNER_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "Villa Construction - Douala",
  "location": "Douala, Cameroon",
  "description": "4-bedroom house construction",
  "budget": "20000000",
  "startDate": "2026-10-01"
}

### 8. Approve that project as Admin (use the project id from step 7)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/PROJECT_ID_2/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "status": "Approved"
}

### 9. Propose an engineer for the approved project (Admin) - professionalId 2 matches the seeded engineer
POST {{baseUrl}}/assignments/propose
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "projectId": PROJECT_ID_2,
  "professionalId": 2
}

### 10. Reject the assignment proposal as Owner (use assignment id from step 9's response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/assignments/ASSIGNMENT_ID/reject
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_OWNER_TOKEN_HERE

### 11. Propose the engineer again (since the first proposal was rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/assignments/propose
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "projectId": PROJECT_ID_2,
  "professionalId": 2
}

### 12. Accept the new assignment proposal as Owner (use the NEW assignment id from step 11)
POST {{baseUrl}}/assignments/ASSIGNMENT_ID_2/accept
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_OWNER_TOKEN_HERE

### 13. Submit a progress report as Engineer
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ENGINEER_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "projectId": "PROJECT_ID_2",
  "summary": "Foundation work completed successfully."
}

### 14. Fetch notifications for Owner
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_OWNER_TOKEN_HERE

### 15. Fetch verified professionals (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/professionals/verified
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
